      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Flowey.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. XP ledger: level 3, power rating 9 → a level 3 Warlock player-character sheet (a player may take this seat; the authored CR 3 stands in where the ledger is silent). Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Repaired-Machine Flower</strong> — Monster Underground / Unknown Royal Remnant</p><p>Status: Active — Mount Ebott arc file needs review</p><p>Flowey is the hostile flower identified by Sans as the twisted remnant of Asgore's dead firstborn son. In Part III, he is also the prime suspect in the overnight repair and deliberate marking of the Legion survey machine.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Friendliness Pellets</strong> — “His soul split apart, each fragment warped beyond recognition.”</li><li><strong>Vine Lash</strong> — “His soul split apart, each fragment warped beyond recognition.”</li><li><strong>Extra Attack</strong> — “His soul split apart, each fragment warped beyond recognition.”</li><li><strong>Burrow</strong> — “After midnight, when the survey team believed him dormant, his mechanical abilities bore fruit: a fully operational Legion machine, scarred but functional, adorned with symbolic markings carved into its chassis.”</li><li><strong>Repaired the Machine</strong> — “In Part III, he is also the prime suspect in the overnight repair and deliberate marking of the Legion survey machine.”</li><li><strong>A Soul in Fragments</strong> — “His soul split apart, each fragment warped beyond recognition.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/flowey</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/flowey</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
